WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Our first guest tonight
is a talented actress

00:00:01.735 --> 00:00:03.169 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know her from her work
on shows like

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:05.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Parks and Recreation"
and FX's "Legion."

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:08.341
She stars in "Black Bear,"
which is in select theater

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:09.809 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and on VOD now.

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:10.577 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's take a look.

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:14.080 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think I'm into traditiona
gender roles.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:17.717 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah. No, I really --
I mean that.

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:18.585 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I don't know.

00:00:18.585 --> 00:00:23.390
Can't say a part of me doesn't
want a man to just come alon

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:26.159 line:92%
and take care of everything.

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:33.066
-Doesn't that kind of contradict
your entire life?

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:35.201 size:81% position:41% line:92%
What about your films?

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:37.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
Don't you think
they're feminist?

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:41.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't think about them
one way or the other.

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:43.977 line:92%
-You don't think about them?

00:00:43.977 --> 00:00:47.180
How can you make something
if you never think about it?

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:50.817 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sometimes when you're makin
something, you're not --

00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:52.752 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-I'm talking to her.

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:54.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Please welcome back
to the show

00:00:54.254 --> 00:00:56.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
our very good friend,
Aubrey Plaza.

00:00:56.523 --> 00:00:58.191 size:75% position:38% line:92%
How are you, Aubrey?

00:00:58.191 --> 00:01:02.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm fine.
How are you, Seth?

00:01:02.462 --> 00:01:04.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you enjoy the Zoom
press, or...?

00:01:04.631 --> 00:01:06.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
I obviously would prefer
if you were here,

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:09.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
but do you like the Zoom
element of it?

00:01:09.202 --> 00:01:12.205 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-I mean, yeah, kind of.

00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:15.642 size:84% position:42%
Although I do feel that
Zoom fatigue is real.

00:01:15.642 --> 00:01:17.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Like, I think it's

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:19.112 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
actually real.

00:01:19.112 --> 00:01:22.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
Every night I am passing out
at 9:00 p.m.

00:01:22.115 --> 00:01:24.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I think my brain
is so stimulated

00:01:24.784 --> 00:01:27.153 size:88% position:44% line:92%
by this -- future Zooms.

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:28.988 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, also you just spend
too much of the day

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:33.226
looking at yourself, which I
think is, like, exhausting

00:01:33.226 --> 00:01:36.429 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's not healthy, it's no
healthy for any of us.

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:38.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know, I don't --
I don't know.

00:01:38.698 --> 00:01:42.402 align:start size:94% position:6%
Screens, robots, they're all
coming for us, Seth.

00:01:42.402 --> 00:01:44.804 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This movie is getting
fantastic reviews.

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:47.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
You are outstanding in it.
It is --

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:49.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
-The three of you,

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:51.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
because it's
basically a three-hander,

00:01:51.845 --> 00:01:54.147 size:78% position:39%
it's just a wonderful
kind of film to watch

00:01:54.147 --> 00:01:55.448 line:92%
because you're all so wonderful,

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:57.283 align:start size:94% position:6%
and there's incredible
shifts in it.

00:01:57.283 --> 00:02:01.354
It seems like it might have been
an exhausting movie to mak

00:02:01.354 --> 00:02:03.289 align:start size:94% position:6%
just because of how,
I don't know,

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:05.425 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, the emotional hoops
you all jump through.

00:02:05.425 --> 00:02:07.727 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Was that the case?

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:10.263 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, it was.
It was...

00:02:10.263 --> 00:02:12.999 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were shooting in a very
remote location

00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:15.635 size:75% position:38%
in middle of nowhere
in the Adirondacks,

00:02:15.635 --> 00:02:20.707 align:start size:94% position:6%
and all night shoots
for 20 days, and I think,

00:02:20.707 --> 00:02:22.942 align:start size:94% position:6%
yeah, I think I totally
lost my mind.

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:26.212 size:81% position:41%
And I think physically
it was very demanding.

00:02:26.212 --> 00:02:27.080 size:78% position:39% line:92%
I was -- I kind of --

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:32.185
My character is, like, basically
wasted for half of the movie

00:02:32.185 --> 00:02:35.221 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I was just
in a constant state of just --

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:36.756 line:92%
I mean, you know how that is

00:02:36.756 --> 00:02:40.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
just being so drunk
that you can't walk upstairs

00:02:40.426 --> 00:02:42.929 align:start size:94% position:6%
without flinging your body
against a wall.

00:02:42.929 --> 00:02:44.464 line:92%
-Yeah, it's like my move.

00:02:44.464 --> 00:02:47.934 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's just your every night.
But, like, I --

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:50.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, I was really --
it was very, very exhausting

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:54.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it felt like --
it was also very joyful

00:02:54.374 --> 00:02:57.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it felt --
I don't know, it was just --

00:02:57.443 --> 00:03:00.780 align:start size:94% position:6%
Christopher Abbott
and Sarah Gadon are so talente

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:05.018
and I think the three of us just
banded together like a weird

00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:09.889
[bleep] family and we just
got through it together.

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:13.526 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was fun,
but in a very dark way.

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:14.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I've been a fan
of Christopher's.

00:03:14.928 --> 00:03:18.565
I had never seen Sarah before.
She's just excellent as well

00:03:18.565 --> 00:03:20.133 line:92%
When you mention night shoots,

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:21.634
you know, I think people
can appreciate that means

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:23.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're shooting at night,
but I think what people forget

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:26.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that means you have to go
back to the real world

00:03:26.239 --> 00:03:27.607 line:92%
at, like, 6:00 in the morning.

00:03:27.607 --> 00:03:30.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, where were you staying
when you shoot

00:03:30.009 --> 00:03:31.978 line:92%
at remote place like this?

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:33.780 line:92%
-Yeah, so we were staying --

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:35.381 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, Chris, Sarah, and I
were staying

00:03:35.381 --> 00:03:37.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
in little town called
Saranac Lake,

00:03:37.584 --> 00:03:39.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
which was about
an hour drive from set.

00:03:39.719 --> 00:03:43.623 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we carpooled together
because the movie had no money

00:03:43.623 --> 00:03:44.924 line:92%
the budget was really small.

00:03:44.924 --> 00:03:48.394 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so we would drive back
to Saranac

00:03:48.394 --> 00:03:51.931 align:start size:94% position:6%
basically as the sun
was coming up,

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:54.167 line:92%
and -- which was our night

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:57.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I remember, like,
you know,

00:03:57.170 --> 00:04:01.407
just to do something normal,
you know, besides shooting

00:04:01.407 --> 00:04:03.710 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would walk around the town
or get a cup of coffee

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:06.179 align:start size:94% position:6%
or whatever, or sit in the par
across from the hotel.

00:04:06.179 --> 00:04:10.984 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I looked so insane
I think most people in the tow

00:04:10.984 --> 00:04:14.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
thought I was like
a crazy street person

00:04:14.621 --> 00:04:18.024 line:92%
that had, like, moved in.

00:04:18.024 --> 00:04:20.493 size:81% position:41% line:92%
And I didn't fight it.

00:04:20.493 --> 00:04:23.029 size:81% position:41% line:92%
I just leaned into it.

00:04:23.029 --> 00:04:26.432 line:92%
And I became this townie.

00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:29.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just -- just --
I looked --

00:04:29.502 --> 00:04:30.837 line:92%
Yeah, I can't explain it.

00:04:30.837 --> 00:04:33.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
I looked on another level
of insane.

00:04:33.106 --> 00:04:35.541 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'd like to think ever
since you left,

00:04:35.541 --> 00:04:37.777 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would like to think
the legend if you in the tow

00:04:37.777 --> 00:04:39.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that you got your act
together.

00:04:39.178 --> 00:04:42.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, for three weeks we had
this crazy woman,

00:04:42.015 --> 00:04:45.151 align:start size:94% position:6%
but then I think
she cleaned herself up.

00:04:45.151 --> 00:04:45.985 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-I cleaned myself up,

00:04:45.985 --> 00:04:49.656 align:start size:94% position:6%
I started acting career
and just immediately got cas

00:04:49.656 --> 00:04:53.459 align:start size:94% position:6%
in two films that came out
in the same week.

00:04:53.459 --> 00:04:55.795 line:92%
Typical rags to riches story

00:04:55.795 --> 00:04:57.430 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The other film,
"Happiest Season,"

00:04:57.430 --> 00:05:01.367 align:start size:94% position:6%
which was a delight,
you filmed in Pittsburgh.

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:03.436 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you enjoy --
I mean, we like to talk abou

00:05:03.436 --> 00:05:04.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
Pittsburgh here
as much as possible.

00:05:04.871 --> 00:05:07.573 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you enjoy
that wonderful city?

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:09.742 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Yes, yes, I loved it.

00:05:09.742 --> 00:05:13.212 size:84% position:42%
And I'm from, you know,
Delaware/Philadelphia.

00:05:13.212 --> 00:05:16.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
So there was a lot
of crossover there,

00:05:16.649 --> 00:05:19.786 line:92%
I feel like, with Philly and -

00:05:19.786 --> 00:05:23.923
[Bleep] I can't remember
the famous sandwich place.

00:05:23.923 --> 00:05:26.626 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Primanti Brothers.

00:05:26.626 --> 00:05:28.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Primanti Brothers?
-Yeah, right?

00:05:28.528 --> 00:05:30.396 align:start size:94% position:6%
The french fries
on the sandwich?

00:05:30.396 --> 00:05:32.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, yes, french fries
on the sandwich.

00:05:32.265 --> 00:05:34.734 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did that.
And I learned very quickly

00:05:34.734 --> 00:05:38.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
that Pittsburgh has, like,
the most amount

00:05:38.538 --> 00:05:40.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
of dive bars or the most
amount of bars,

00:05:40.139 --> 00:05:42.675 align:start size:94% position:6%
I guess, in their city.
-Yeah, it's a pretty bar city.

00:05:42.675 --> 00:05:46.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's crazy.
So that was very fun.

00:05:46.846 --> 00:05:50.583 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we frequented
a lot of those places.

00:05:50.583 --> 00:05:53.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
And also, just the city
is beautiful.

00:05:53.286 --> 00:05:55.755
I never -- I had never bee
there, so I didn't realize

00:05:55.755 --> 00:05:58.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
like -- it was almost European
with all the bridges

00:05:58.858 --> 00:06:03.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the waterways,
and I loved it.

00:06:03.096 --> 00:06:04.397 line:92%
I'd love to go back there.

00:06:04.397 --> 00:06:07.300
-I want to also -- You mentioned
that you're from Delaware.

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:09.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
I do feel like people
from who are from Delaware

00:06:09.302 --> 00:06:10.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
also always say
a second place.

00:06:10.837 --> 00:06:13.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, "I'm from
Delaware/Philadelphia."

00:06:13.239 --> 00:06:15.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
But this is a big time
for Delaware.

00:06:15.441 --> 00:06:16.442 line:92%
-Okay, I'm not belittling --

00:06:16.442 --> 00:06:18.544 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, we have
a Delaware president.

00:06:18.544 --> 00:06:21.013 line:92%
Are you very excited about that?

00:06:21.013 --> 00:06:23.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, I love Joe.
I love --

00:06:23.216 --> 00:06:24.984 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm very, very
excited about it.

00:06:24.984 --> 00:06:28.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was campaigning for him.
I was out there.

00:06:28.755 --> 00:06:30.890 size:75% position:38% line:92%
And I really feel --

00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:32.492 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've known him
since I was 16.

00:06:32.492 --> 00:06:35.495
I don't know him well, but I met
him when I was a teenager,

00:06:35.495 --> 00:06:38.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I think most people
in Wilmington have met him

00:06:38.631 --> 00:06:39.766 line:92%
at one point or the other.

00:06:39.766 --> 00:06:43.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's just that kind of guy
he's very approachable.

00:06:43.636 --> 00:06:46.172 size:78% position:39% line:92%
And I'm just psyched.

00:06:46.172 --> 00:06:47.240 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Like, I think it's cool.

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:49.175 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Delaware's never
had a president,

00:06:49.175 --> 00:06:50.143 line:92%
so it's, like, about time.

00:06:50.143 --> 00:06:53.045
We're the first state, you know,
if you didn't know that.

00:06:53.045 --> 00:06:55.314 align:start size:94% position:6%
We signed --
we got on there first.

00:06:55.314 --> 00:06:58.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were like,
"Yeah, we'll be a state."

00:06:58.017 --> 00:07:01.587 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's just a big moment
for my hometown,

00:07:01.587 --> 00:07:03.656 line:92%
so I'm very excited about it

00:07:03.656 --> 00:07:05.458 align:start size:94% position:6%
-If someone said,
"I'm going to Wilmington.

00:07:05.458 --> 00:07:07.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
Where should I go?"
Where would you tell them?

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:09.362
Because I feel like Primanti
Brothers is a perfect exampl

00:07:09.362 --> 00:07:11.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
of where you tell someone
to go if they're in Pittsburgh

00:07:11.697 --> 00:07:14.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
What is the equivalent
in Wilmington?

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:18.971 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, I guess
the equivalent...

00:07:18.971 --> 00:07:21.340 line:92%
I mean, honestly, there's...

00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:24.610
Delaware is the kind of plac
you have to find your own --

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:26.579 line:92%
You have to find your own fun.

00:07:26.579 --> 00:07:28.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Um, one --

00:07:28.614 --> 00:07:31.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
One thing that I used to d
growing up,

00:07:31.584 --> 00:07:34.086 size:84% position:42%
and I think the kids
still do it these days,

00:07:34.086 --> 00:07:35.922 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's called
cruising the Pike.

00:07:35.922 --> 00:07:37.623 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
-This basically means

00:07:37.623 --> 00:07:42.261
you get in your car and you just
drive up and down Route 202,

00:07:42.261 --> 00:07:44.197 line:92%
which is called Concorde Pike.

00:07:44.197 --> 00:07:45.898 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's just a bunch
of strip malls.

00:07:45.898 --> 00:07:47.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's great.
-You got your standard --

00:07:47.233 --> 00:07:49.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So it's basically
like an escape room?

00:07:49.602 --> 00:07:54.040 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, but sometimes
I would wear giant --

00:07:54.040 --> 00:07:55.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would wear giant
bear costumes

00:07:55.808 --> 00:07:57.743 size:81% position:41%
or different costumes
and I would just stand

00:07:57.743 --> 00:08:02.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
on the side of the highway
and just wave.

00:08:02.548 --> 00:08:05.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, you have to be
creative there.

00:08:05.351 --> 00:08:08.354
A lot of [bleep] goes down
in the Wawa parking lot.

00:08:08.354 --> 00:08:10.990 size:84% position:42%
I would suggest going
to the Wawa parking lot

00:08:10.990 --> 00:08:14.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I would also suggest going
to Trolley Square,

00:08:14.293 --> 00:08:17.630 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is where a bunch
of bars are,

00:08:17.630 --> 00:08:20.099 line:92%
and that is a real scene.

00:08:20.099 --> 00:08:22.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
Trolleywood is what
we're calling it now.

00:08:22.235 --> 00:08:25.304 size:78% position:39%
-Well, you've painted
a beautiful picture.

00:08:25.304 --> 00:08:25.805 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, yes.

00:08:25.805 --> 00:08:27.273 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It is always so nice
to see you.

00:08:27.273 --> 00:08:28.774 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Congrats on both films

00:08:28.774 --> 00:08:30.610 line:92%
and I hope to see you soon

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:31.711 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Thank you, Seth.

00:08:31.711 --> 00:08:33.513
Thank you so much for having me.
-[ Laughing ]

00:08:33.513 --> 00:08:34.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I love you so much
and I just --

00:08:34.914 --> 00:08:37.083 align:start size:94% position:6%
I really -- I miss you.
I miss you.

00:08:37.083 --> 00:08:39.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I wish I could come to
New York and see you sometime.

00:08:39.185 --> 00:08:40.820
-"Black Bear" is in select
theaters and on VOD now.

00:08:40.820 --> 00:08:43.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
We'll be back with
more "Late Night."

